NETWORK TOPOLOGY

The network consists of four Cisco 2960 switches connected in a hierarchical topology, with six end devices connected to the central switch.

SWITCH CONFIGURATION
- Switch0 (S1): Configured as VTP Server.
- Switch1 (S2): Configured as VTP Transparent.
- Switch2 (S3): Configured as VTP Client.
- Switch3 (S4): Configured as VTP Client.

VLAN SEGMENTATION
Three VLANs are configured to separate devices based on departments:

- VLAN 10 – Students: PC0 and PC1.
- VLAN 20 – Staff: PC2 and Laptop0.
- VLAN 30 – HOD: Laptop1 and PC3.

NETWORK CONNECTIVITY
- All six end devices are connected to Switch0.
- Switch0 is connected to Switch1 through a trunk link.
- Switch1 connects to Switch2 and Switch3 through separate trunk links.
- VTP is used to demonstrate VLAN management and advertisement forwarding across the switching network.

NOTE
The topology diagram shows the physical connections and intended switch roles. Trunk operation and VTP propagation should be verified separately in Packet Tracer before being reported as successful.
